CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced as int: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
inconsistent deduction
--
A constexpr static data member (template) of class type was not const
([dcl.constexpr]/6), so the member read in the if constexpr condition did
not fold, both branches were kept and the discarded `return 1.0' took
part in the deduction.  On MSVC this made ranges::iter_move return void
for `int *&', so indirectly_readable<int *> and every iterator concept
above it were false (std::span's iterator constructor).
